From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Pedro Maione <pedro.maione@9elements.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] arm: dts: ast2700-evb: mux the FMC quad SPI pins

The FMC flashes are read with four data lines, but nothing muxes the
FWQSPI pins (M16 and A15) that carry IO2 and IO3. This only works when
an earlier boot stage has set them. On AST2700 A1 the BootMCU firmware
reads the boot flash in single mode and leaves them unset, so every
quad read through the FMC window returns garbage and bootspi fails with
FDT_ERR_BADMAGIC.

Select the FWQSPI function for the FMC, as the ASPEED SDK device tree
does.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Pedro Maione <pedro.maione@9elements.com>
---
 arch/arm/dts/ast2700-evb.dts | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm/dts/ast2700-evb.dts b/arch/arm/dts/ast2700-evb.dts
index e7222d9691f..fc8d6955d7e 100644
--- a/arch/arm/dts/ast2700-evb.dts
+++ b/arch/arm/dts/ast2700-evb.dts
@@ -58,8 +58,17 @@
 	tx-internal-delay-ps = <0>;
 };
 
+&pinctrl1 {
+	pinctrl_fwqspi_default: fwqspi-default {
+		function = "FWQSPI";
+		groups = "FWQSPI";
+	};
+};
+
 &fmc {
 	status = "okay";
+	pinctrl-names = "default";
+	pinctrl-0 = <&pinctrl_fwqspi_default>;
 
 	flash@0 {
 		status = "okay";
